msgctxt "164"
msgid "Shall we go, Kiryu-sama?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "176"
msgid "Ah. You must be Kazuma Kiryu-sama."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "188"
msgid "Yeah. And you're Tamiya's driver, right?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "200"
msgid "Actually, his secretary. You can call me Higaki, sir."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "212"
msgid "And you. You're from... the media, yes?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "224"
msgid ""
"Yup. Name's Date, from the Keihin News. Used to hang my hat\r\n"
"with the force though. That's how I know Kiryu."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "236"
msgid "I'm sorry, sir, but I'm afraid I can't allow a reporter to⑬"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "248"
msgid ""
"Now hold your horses. What we have here is a prominent government official "
"arranging a private meeting with the ex-chairman of a major crime syndicate."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "260"
msgid ""
"If you don't let me come, I'll have to write an article based on that info "
"alone. And who knows what kind of conclusions I could draw from that."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "272"
msgid "But..."
msgstr "Ma..."

msgctxt "284"
msgid ""
"Sorry, but I think it's for the best if you let Date-san come with us. We "
"promise he won't write about anything he hears today. Right, Date-san?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "296"
msgid "Yeah, sure."
msgstr "Sì, certo."

msgctxt "308"
msgid "...Very well, then. Please get in the car when you're ready, sir."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "320"
msgid "I actually still have one or two things I need to do first. Sorry."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "332"
msgid "No need to apologize, sir."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "344"
msgid "Just please, make it quick."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "356"
msgid "All right, let's go."
msgstr "Va bene, andiamo."

msgctxt "368"
msgid "Very well, sir. Just get in the car and we'll be on our way."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "392"
msgid "Not yet."
msgstr "Non ancora."

msgctxt "404"
msgid "Yeah, I'm ready."
msgstr "Sì, sono pronto."

msgctxt "416"
msgid "Don't Get In"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "428"
msgid "Get In"
msgstr "Entra."

